      "description": "Newly built family home in Hertfordshire\n\nA 3,000 sq ft new-build in Hertfordshire, designed for a family who wanted the house to feel full of personality and depth despite starting with little architectural detail or character of its own. Selway Design Studio drew colour straight from the grounds beyond, bringing the green of the surrounding landscape into the home, while furnishings in the studio's signature style — mixing eras and layering old against new — build the depth the architecture alone couldn't provide. Natural materials warm the kitchen at the heart of the home, with every choice weighed against the existing architecture so nothing ever felt pastiche or out of place."
    },
    {
      "slug": "maya-fine-jewellery",
      "title": "maya fine jewellery",
      "description": "Feminine and ethereal Jewel Box of a Showroom, London\n\nA jewellery showroom in Bloomsbury, London for fine jewellery designer Maya Selway, conceived as an immersive retail environment for a high-net-worth clientele. Selway Design Studio designed the space to evoke the intimacy and tactility of a jewellery box, enveloping visitors in a rich, layered material experience. Warm timber tones, soft textiles and sculptural surfaces create depth and atmosphere, allowing the jewellery to sit within a calm, considered architectural backdrop. Bespoke display elements and carefully controlled lighting enhance the perception of craft and detail, supporting a slower, more intimate way of engaging with the work — a showroom that reflects Maya Selway's own sensibility, balancing material richness with restraint.",
