      "title": "nile street",
      "description": "A thoughtful renovation in Austin, Texas for private clients\n\nDesigned as a calm and materially expressive urban home. Selway Design Studio in collaboration with Benjamin Stelly reworked the kitchen and dining space as the heart of the home, balancing functionality with a refined, layered aesthetic. Lighting plays a defining role, with sculptural fixtures by Volker Haug, WDSTCK and Thorup Copenhagen establishing atmosphere and rhythm across the space.\n\nA rich material palette of oak, black soapstone and aged brass creates contrast and depth, with bespoke joinery and moss-green accents softening the architectural lines. Custom banquette seating frames the dining area, while integrated artwork introduces a more personal, curated dimension — a quietly expressive, enduring interior where light, material and form work together.",
