      "title": "xabia",
      "description": "mediterranean family apartment renovation in Jávea, Spain\n\nA Mediterranean family home renovation in Jávea, Spain. Originally purchased by Tanya's grandparents in the 1970s, the apartment has long served as a family retreat, with this renovation focused on preserving its retro character while introducing a more considered, layered interior.\n\nSelway Design Studio embraced the home's original charm, combining 1970s references with subtle English influences through striped textiles, soft furnishings and curated details. A deep-blue mosaic bathroom introduces a bold, high-contrast moment, while an original 1970s modular sofa and rattan bar define the living space, balancing comfort with a relaxed coastal sensibility.\n\nArtworks by Tanya and her family are displayed throughout, bringing a personal, generational narrative into the interiors — a highly expressive home that balances nostalgia, craftsmanship and a distinctly Mediterranean way of living.",
